## Prompt Design Considerations

Self-consistency doesn't require a special prompt format — use a standard few-shot CoT prompt. A few things help:

**Use diverse, high-quality CoT examples.** The examples themselves influence the range of reasoning strategies the model tries. If all examples use the same approach, the sampled paths will be less diverse.

**Temperature tuning.** Too low (< 0.3) → paths are too similar, less benefit. Too high (> 1.0) → paths become incoherent. 0.5–0.8 is a good starting range.

**Consistent answer format in examples.** The extraction step (Step 3) is easier when answers are in a predictable location, e.g., always ending with "The answer is X." Make this explicit in your CoT examples.

